    "answer": {
      "short": "$OX=OY$ and $MN\\perp XY$.\n\nUse the equal circle radii to establish congruent triangles; the equal angles at $O$ lie on a straight line, so each is $90^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "The circle radii give $XM=YM=XY$ and $XN=YN=XY$, so $\\triangle XMY$ and $\\triangle XNY$ are equilateral. Thus $\\angle NXM=\\angle NYM=120^\\circ$.\n\nAlso, $XM=YM$, $XN=YN$ and $MN=MN$, so $\\triangle XMN\\cong\\triangle YMN$ by SSS. Hence $MN$ bisects $\\angle XMY=60^\\circ$, giving $\\angle XMO=\\angle YMO=30^\\circ$.\n\nIn $\\triangle XMO$ and $\\triangle YMO$:\n$$\\begin{align*}XM&=YM &&\\text{(equal radii)}\\\\ \\angle XMO&=\\angle YMO &&\\text{(established above)}\\\\ MO&=MO &&\\text{(shared side)}\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $\\triangle XMO\\cong\\triangle YMO$ by SAS. Corresponding parts give $OX=OY$ and $\\angle XOM=\\angle YOM$.\n\nSince $X$, $O$ and $Y$ lie on a straight line,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle XOM+\\angle YOM&=180^\\circ\\\\ 2\\angle XOM&=180^\\circ\\\\ \\angle XOM&=90^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $MN\\perp XY$, and $O$ is the midpoint of $XY$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
